{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"core-argument","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":450,"height":280,"text":"# Core Argument\n\n**Primary Claim:** [The paper's central claim — one sentence]\n\n**Logical Chain:**\n1. [Premise / evidence 1]\n2. [Premise / evidence 2]\n3. [Premise / evidence 3]\n→ **Therefore:** [Conclusion]\n\n**Argument Type:** [Causal / mechanistic / correlational / descriptive]\n\n**Key Evidence:** [The single strongest piece of evidence, with numbers]","color":"1"},
		{"id":"assumptions","type":"text","x":500,"y":0,"width":400,"height":300,"text":"# Assumptions\n\n**Explicit Assumptions:**\n1. [Assumption the authors state — quote if possible]\n2. [Another stated assumption]\n\n**Implicit Assumptions:**\n1. [Hidden assumption needed for the argument to work]\n2. [Another unstated assumption]\n\n**Most Questionable:** [Which assumption, if wrong, would most damage the conclusions? Why?]","color":"2"},
		{"id":"evidence-assessment","type":"text","x":950,"y":0,"width":400,"height":300,"text":"# Evidence Assessment\n\n**Strongest Evidence:**\n- [Finding + stat support]\n- [Finding + stat support]\n\n**Weakest Evidence:**\n- [Finding + why it's weak]\n\n**Critical Gap:** [The most important missing evidence]\n\n**Replication:** [Are key findings replicated within the paper? Across papers?]","color":"3"},
		{"id":"alternative-explanations","type":"text","x":0,"y":330,"width":450,"height":280,"text":"# Alternative Explanations\n\n**Competing Hypotheses:**\n1. [Alternative explanation 1]\n2. [Alternative explanation 2]\n\n**Could Confounding Explain This?**\n[Most serious confound and whether the design controls for it]\n\n**Plausibility vs. Authors' Claim:**\n[Are the alternatives MORE or LESS plausible? Why?]","color":"4"},
		{"id":"methodological-critique","type":"text","x":500,"y":350,"width":400,"height":280,"text":"# Methodological Critique\n\n**Strongest Design Choice:**\n[Specific choice + why it strengthens the evidence]\n\n**Most Serious Limitation:**\n[Limitation + which validity it threatens: internal/external/construct/statistical conclusion]\n\n**Limitations NOT Discussed:**\n[At least one the authors don't acknowledge]\n\n**Statistical Concerns:**\n[Power, multiplicity, model assumptions, p-hacking risk]","color":"5"},
		{"id":"personal-relevance","type":"text","x":950,"y":350,"width":400,"height":280,"text":"# Personal Relevance\n\n**Connections to My Research:**\n- [Specific link to your work]\n- [Specific link to your work]\n\n**What I Can Use:**\n- [Method/protocol/finding directly applicable]\n\n**What This Changes for Me:**\n[Does this support, challenge, or complicate your existing understanding?]","color":"6"},
		{"id":"future-directions","type":"text","x":0,"y":660,"width":450,"height":280,"text":"# Future Directions\n\n**Immediate (1-2 years):**\n1. [Specific follow-up study]\n2. [Specific follow-up study]\n\n**Medium-term (3-5 years):**\n1. [Research program direction]\n\n**The Most Important Unanswered Question:**\n[One question + what study design would answer it]","color":"7"},
		{"id":"critical-questions-enhanced","type":"text","x":500,"y":680,"width":400,"height":280,"text":"# Critical Questions\n\n**What Would Falsify the Hypothesis?**\n[Specific result that would prove it wrong]\n\n**Where Is the Argument Weakest?**\n[The step in the logical chain with least support]\n\n**What Are the Boundary Conditions?**\n[When/where/for whom does this NOT apply?]\n\n**What's the Minimum Evidence Needed for Confidence?**\n[What would it take for you to believe this?]","color":"8"},
		{"id":"hypothesis-center","type":"text","x":950,"y":680,"width":400,"height":280,"text":"# Re-evaluated Hypothesis\n\n**Updated Understanding:**\n[Your synthesis after working through all 8 nodes above]\n\n**Innovation:** [High/Med/Low] — [Why?]\n**Evidence:** [High/Med/Low] — [Why?]\n**Practical Potential:** [High/Med/Low] — [Why?]\n\n**Remaining Uncertainties:**\n[What you still don't know or trust]","color":"9"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"edge-1","fromNode":"core-argument","fromSide":"right","toNode":"assumptions","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"edge-2","fromNode":"core-argument","fromSide":"right","toNode":"evidence-assessment","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"edge-3","fromNode":"assumptions","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"alternative-explanations","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"edge-4","fromNode":"evidence-assessment","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"alternative-explanations","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"edge-5","fromNode":"alternative-explanations","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"methodological-critique","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"edge-6","fromNode":"methodological-critique","fromSide":"right","toNode":"personal-relevance","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"edge-7","fromNode":"personal-relevance","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"future-directions","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"edge-8","fromNode":"future-directions","fromSide":"right","toNode":"critical-questions-enhanced","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"edge-9","fromNode":"critical-questions-enhanced","fromSide":"right","toNode":"hypothesis-center","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"edge-10","fromNode":"hypothesis-center","fromSide":"top","toNode":"core-argument","toSide":"bottom"}
	]
}
